  UniqueResponseToPlayerDisplayTexts:
  - name_: Angry Observation
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 0
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 4
    displayTexts:
    - 'In the center of the room lies a makeshift graveyard and prayer site. A group
      of robed men kneels around the tombstones, praying under their breath. You
      notice that beneath the hoods, they all look the same but of different ages.
      "May the Hand of Spawn recognize that these fallen have given so much to it.
      That the next version of them be stronger so they can serve you better. Their
      weakness is not celebrated but learned. For there is much to improve to serve
      the Spawns." '
    - You clench your fists. How dreadful these people live. How dare they live to
      suppress our humanity? The words "The Shifts" drift in your mind, though you
      have no clear understanding of their meaning. All you know is their serving
      of an oppressive rule and their willingness to be sheep to a system that wants
      their demise.
  - name_: Sad Observation
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 1
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 4
    displayTexts:
    - 'In the center of the room lies a makeshift graveyard and prayer site. A group
      of robed men kneels around the tombstones, praying under their breath. You
      notice that beneath the hoods, they all look the same but of different ages.
      "May the Hand of Spawn recognize that these fallen have given so much to it.
      That the next version of them be stronger so they can serve you better. Their
      weakness is not celebrated but learned. For there is much to improve to serve
      the Spawns." '
    - Sadness compels you to shed a tear for these unfortunate men. "The Shifts,"
      you are reminded of. Beyond these words, they dedicate their lives to their
      oppressive ruler. So sad that people are so craving meaning that they will
      follow anybody or anything just to feel seen.
  - name_: Joy Observation
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 2
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 4
    displayTexts:
    - 'In the center of the room lies a makeshift graveyard and prayer site. A group
      of robed men kneels around the tombstones, praying under their breath. You
      notice that beneath the hoods, they all look the same but of different ages.
      "May the Hand of Spawn recognize that these fallen have given so much to it.
      That the next version of them be stronger so they can serve you better. Their
      weakness is not celebrated but learned. For there is much to improve to serve
      the Spawns." '
    - A smile draws across your face. Seeing such a wonderful celebration of how
      we can all be better at serving the Hand of the Spawn. The words "The Shifts"
      remind you of their identity. How wonderful that we can all work harder.
  - name_: Fear Observation
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 3
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 4
    displayTexts:
    - 'In the center of the room lies a makeshift graveyard and prayer site. A group
      of robed men kneels around the tombstones, praying under their breath. You
      notice that beneath the hoods, they all look the same but of different ages.
      "May the Hand of Spawn recognize that these fallen have given so much to it.
      That the next version of them be stronger so they can serve you better. Their
      weakness is not celebrated but learned. For there is much to improve to serve
      the Spawns." '
    - 'A nervousness twinges your muscles. The Hand of Spawn shall not be messed
      with, your mind says. You agree despite not understanding its content. Your
      mind continues: The Shifts, the group here, pray mainly out of fear. But when
      one of them finally prays out of faith and strength, then freedom shall be
      granted to that perfect vessel.'
  - name_: Fear Manipulate
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 3
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 5
    displayTexts:
    - At the center of the room are the robed men, praying at the graveyard. An anger
      takes hold of you. "The Shifts", your mind calls them. A despicable group that
      serves to undermine our uniqueness into a single value number.  To serve an
      oppressive Hand of Spawn. You look to see if you can take something from them.
      You venture closer and attempt to steal something.
    - However, the Hand of Spawn frightens you too much to follow through with this
      pickpocket.
  - name_: Joy Manipulate
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 2
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 5
    displayTexts:
    - At the center of the room are the robed men, praying at the graveyard. An anger
      takes hold of you. "The Shifts", your mind calls them. A despicable group that
      serves to undermine our uniqueness into a single value number.  To serve an
      oppressive Hand of Spawn. You look to see if you can take something from them.
      You venture closer and attempt to steal something.
    - Happiness enlightens you. The Shifts, your mind tells you, have such a wonderful
      purpose to serve the Hand of Spawn. To better themselves to be Valued and to
      become the best Vessel for the Spawns. You cannot bring yourself to steal from
      these people.
  - name_: Sad Manipulate
    UseEmotionKey: 1
    emotionKey: 1
    UseMotorSensorKey: 1
    motorSensorKey: 5
    displayTexts:
    - At the center of the room are the robed men, praying at the graveyard. An anger
      takes hold of you. "The Shifts", your mind calls them. A despicable group that
      serves to undermine our uniqueness into a single value number.  To serve an
      oppressive Hand of Spawn. You look to see if you can take something from them.
      You venture closer and attempt to steal something.
    - 'A pitiful sadness takes over. Your mind tells you: The Shifts have become
      manipulated to find purpose only in this purposeless cause. To throw themselves
      at becoming a pawn in this oppressive system. You cannot bring yourself to
      steal from such pitiful people.'
  allActionsOnObject: []
